    "created_at": "2016-09-15T15:37:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-09-15T15:37:36Z",
    "body": "For the longest time I knew blink and webkit implemented the abort downstream of the bindings without ever giving much thought to this script-observable side-effect.  I've never seen any bug reports about this interop issue, so I am not too worried about braking the web by going either way.  So the question is, what is the right thing to do here?\n\nThe idea of WebIDL extension is appealing. Would it make sense to have something like that in the spec?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
