    "created_at": "2016-09-15T15:58:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-09-15T15:58:29Z",
    "body": "Hmm, I tend to disagree that it's reasonable to add to IDL. It'd be a kind of strange unprecedented type conversion, which aborts the subsequent algorithm without throwing an exception. Just inlining the steps into the start of each method makes more sense to me.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
